<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Lutter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1626">1626</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Lutter am Barenberge · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Lutter was fought on 27 August 1626 near Lutter am Barenberge in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a> army under Count Tilly defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-iv-of-denmark">Christian IV of Denmark</a>, who had entered the war as leader of the Protestant cause in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. The defeat led to imperial occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jutland">Jutland</a> and to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-lubeck">Treaty of Lübeck</a> of 1629, which ended Danish intervention.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-lutter.jpg" alt="Battle of Lutter" width="320" height="276" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Caspar Lundorp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schlacht_bei_Lutter_am_Barenberge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
